Lec 30-3
 
 
 
CURL IN 3D
 
For a vector field \vec{F} = P\hat{i} + Q\hat{j} + R\hat{k}:
\operatorname{curl} \vec{F} = (R_y - Q_z)\hat{i} + (P_z - R_x)\hat{j} + (Q_x - P_y)\hat{k}
 
Key Theorem
 
If \vec{F} is defined in a simply-connected region:
\vec{F} \text{ is conservative} \iff \operatorname{curl} \vec{F} = \vec{0}
 
 
 
∇ Operator Recap
 
\nabla = \left\langle \frac{\partial}{\partial x}, \frac{\partial}{\partial y}, \frac{\partial}{\partial z} \right\rangle
 
- Gradient:
\nabla f = \left\langle \frac{\partial f}{\partial x}, \frac{\partial f}{\partial y}, \frac{\partial f}{\partial z} \right\rangle
- Divergence:
\nabla \cdot \langle P, Q, R \rangle = \frac{\partial P}{\partial x} + \frac{\partial Q}{\partial y} + \frac{\partial R}{\partial z} = \operatorname{div} \vec{F}
 
Curl via Cross Product
 
$$\nabla \times \vec{F} = \begin{vmatrix}
\hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \
\frac{\partial}{\partial x} & \frac{\partial}{\partial y} & \frac{\partial}{\partial z} \
P & Q & R
\end{vmatrix}
= \left( \frac{\partial R}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial Q}{\partial z} \right)\hat{i}
 
- \left( \frac{\partial R}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial P}{\partial z} \right)\hat{j}
 
- \left( \frac{\partial Q}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial P}{\partial y} \right)\hat{k}
= \operatorname{curl} \vec{F}$$
 
 
 
Geometric Interpretation
 
"Curl measures the rotation component in a velocity field."
 
- Rotation about the z-axis at angular velocity \omega:
\vec{V} = \langle -\omega y, \omega x, 0 \rangle \implies \operatorname{curl} \vec{V} = 2\omega \hat{k}
 
 
 
