- Critical points: Solve \nabla f = \mathbf{0}.
- Second derivative test: Classifies critical points as local minimum, local maximum, or saddle point.
- Also check values of f on the boundary and as x \to \infty.
 
 
 
Max/Min with Non-Independent Variables (g = c)
 
