\begin{cases}
\nabla f = \lambda \nabla g \\
g = c
\end{cases}

- Note: The second derivative test does not apply here.
 
 
 
Constrained Partial Derivatives
 
Given constraint g(x, y, z) = c, compute \frac{\partial f}{\partial x}:
 
- Formal partial derivative: x varies, y, z held constant.
- \left(\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}\right)_y: y held constant, z depends on x, y, x varies.
- \left(\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}\right)_z: y depends on x, z.
 
 
 
