Polar Coordinates
 
- Area element: dA = r \, dr \, d\theta
- Example: Circle r = 2\cos\theta
- Cartesian form: (x-1)^2 + y^2 = 1
- Derived from r^2 - 2r\cos\theta = 0 \implies r = 2\cos\theta
- Integral: \int_{\theta = -\pi/2}^{\pi/2} \int_{r=0}^{2\cos\theta} f(\cdots) r \, dr \, d\theta
 
Change of Variables to uv-Coordinates
 
- Jacobian determinant:

\frac{\partial(u, v)}{\partial(x, y)} = \begin{vmatrix}
u_x & u_y \\
v_x & v_y
\end{vmatrix}

- Area element transformation:

du \, dv = \left|\frac{\partial(u, v)}{\partial(x, y)}\right| dx \, dy

