Triple Integrals
 
Volume Elements
 
- Rectangular coordinates: dV = dz \, dy \, dx
- Cylindrical coordinates: dV = dz \, r \, dr \, d\theta
- Spherical coordinates: dV = \rho^2 \sin\phi \, d\rho \, d\phi \, d\theta
 
Applications
 
- Area/Volume/Mass:
\iint 1 \, dA, \iiint 1 \, dV, \iiint \delta \, dA or \iiint \delta \, dV
- Average value of a function f:
\bar{f} = \frac{1}{\text{Vol}} \iiint_D f \, dV, or weighted average: \frac{1}{\text{Mass}} \iiint f \delta \, dV
- Center of mass: (\bar{x}, \bar{y}, \bar{z})
- Moment of inertia: I_z = \iiint (x^2 + y^2) \delta \, dV
