Work and Line Integrals (in plane and space)
 
- Line integral: \int_C \vec{F} \cdot d\vec{r} = \int_C M \, dx + N \, dy
where \vec{F} = \langle M, N \rangle. Express x and y in terms of a single parameter.
 
Gradient Fields & Path Independence
 
- If \operatorname{curl} \vec{F} = \mathbf{0} and \vec{F} is defined in a simply-connected region, then \vec{F} is a gradient field: \vec{F} = \nabla f for some scalar function f.
- In 2D: 1 condition N_x = M_y
- In 3D: 3 conditions

